module idd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.idaho.{ frcp6-idaho }

// The District of Idaho's own periods, computed under the federal rules
// (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). Most apply "unless otherwise
// ordered" where the rule says so, and the court may shorten or extend any
// of them for cause (Loc. Civ. R. 6.1). Rules that state no period or
// limit stay out, as do these: the scheduling order within the earlier of
// 90 days after service or 60 days after appearance (Loc. Civ. R. 16.1(a)),
// which restates FRCP 16(b)(2) and binds the court; initial disclosures
// within 14 days of the Rule 26(f) conference (Loc. Civ. R. 16.1(a)(1)),
// FRCP 26(a)(1)(C)'s own period; the trial memorandum "within fourteen
// (14) calendar days before the scheduled trial date" (Loc. Civ. R.
// 16.3(b)), which reads as a window as well as a deadline and is left a
// hole; the mediator's report within 7 days of the last session (Loc. Civ.
// R. 16.4(b)(3)(F)), a mediator's duty; the attorney fee motion within 14
// days after entry of judgment (Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(b)), which restates FRCP
// 54(d)(2)(B) and is lit/frcp's (fees.lit); the two years after entry for
// a joint acknowledgment of satisfaction (Loc. Civ. R. 58.2); execution
// "after fourteen (14) days from the entry of a judgment" (Loc. Civ. R.
// 62.1(c)), which yields to FRCP 62 and is an earliest date, not a
// deadline; the 14 days' notice before summary judgment against a surety
// (Loc. Civ. R. 65.1(a)), a term of the bond; the show-cause periods the
// court sets by order on a felony conviction (Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(2)(A),
// (B)); the 14-day wind-up after reciprocal discipline (Loc. Civ. R.
// 83.5(b)(3)(B)), a grace period and not a filing; the 21 days after a
// withdrawal order in which no proceeding may affect the client (Loc. Civ.
// R. 83.6(c)(4)), a stay rather than a deadline; and the capital habeas
// brief lengths (Loc. Civ. R. 9.2(o)(3)), which the parties may change by
// stipulation. No fee is stated. The earlier D. Idaho outline's FRCP flow
// and its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v.
// Liberty Lobby, Reeves, Catlin, Bowles, Hamer) are FRCP and FRAP
// authority and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap; its Ninth Circuit
// decisions (Eitel v. McCool; Lopez v. Smith) are removed: no reporter
// text is vendored.
/// A memorandum of points and authorities supporting or opposing a motion,
/// including the separate brief that accompanies a motion and the response
/// brief: at most 20 pages without express leave of court, granted only
/// under unusual circumstances (Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2), (b)(1), (c)(1)).
limit memorandum {
  pages <= 20 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2)"

/// A reply brief: at most 10 pages (Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2), (b)(3)).
limit reply-memorandum {
  pages <= 10 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(a)(2)"

/// The separate statement of material facts the moving party contends are
/// not in dispute, or the responding party contends are in dispute, on a
/// motion for summary judgment: at most 10 pages (Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(1),
/// (c)(2)).
limit statement-of-facts {
  pages <= 10 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(1)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(1)"

/// A notice of supplemental authority: at most two pages (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 7.1(d)(2)).
limit supplemental-authority-notice {
  pages <= 2 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(d)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(d)"

/// A trial memorandum: at most 20 pages (Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(b)).
limit trial-memorandum {
  pages <= 20 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(b)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(b)"

/// A response to the opposing parties' trial memoranda: at most 10 pages
/// (Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c)).
limit trial-response-memorandum {
  pages <= 10 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c)"

/// Objections to a magistrate judge's order or report and recommendation,
/// and a response to another party's objections: at most 20 pages (Loc.
/// Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1), (2)).
limit magistrate-objection {
  pages <= 20 cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)"
} cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)"

/// The complaint is filed (Loc. Civ. R. 4.1).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// A party receives an electronically filed document, or notice of its
/// filing, whichever first occurs (Loc. Civ. R. 5.1(e)).
event ElectronicFilingReceived()
/// The moving party's memorandum of points and authorities is served
/// (Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(1), (c)(1)).
event MotionMemorandumServed() paper memorandum
/// The responding party's memorandum is served on the moving party (Loc.
/// Civ. R. 7.1(b)(3), (c)(1)).
event ResponseMemorandumServed() paper memorandum
/// The order granting a motion to amend or supplement a pleading under FRCP
/// 15(a)(2) or (d) is entered (Loc. Civ. R. 15.1(b)).
event AmendmentGranted()
/// The Rule 16 scheduling conference is held at the time and date set
/// (Loc. Civ. R. 16.1(a), 16.4(c)).
event SchedulingConferenceHeld()
/// Trial is scheduled to commence (Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(a), 47.1(a), 51.1,
/// 54.3).
event TrialBegins()
/// The opposing parties' trial memoranda are served (Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c)).
event TrialMemorandumServed() paper trial-memorandum
/// A judgment under which costs may be claimed is entered (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 54.1(a)(1)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A party serves its cost bill (Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(a)(2)).
event CostBillServed()
/// The clerk taxes costs (Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(c)(1)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// A party receives a motion for allowance of attorney fees (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 54.2(c)).
event FeeMotionReceived() paper memorandum
/// The moving party receives the response brief on a motion for attorney
/// fees (Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(d)).
event FeeResponseReceived() paper memorandum
/// Counsel receives the last Notice of Award necessary to calculate the
/// total amount of retroactive benefits (Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(a)).
event LastNoticeOfAwardReceived()
/// The claimant or the defendant receives a motion for attorney fees under
/// 42 U.S.C. §§ 406(b) or 1383(d)(2) (Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c)).
event SocialSecurityFeeMotionReceived() paper memorandum
/// A response brief on a motion for attorney fees under 42 U.S.C. §§ 406(b)
/// or 1383(d)(2) is filed (Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c)).
event SocialSecurityFeeResponseFiled() paper memorandum
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's nondispositive order (Loc.
/// Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1)).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's report and recommendation
/// (Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(2)).
event MagistrateReportServed()
/// A party is served with another party's objections to a magistrate
/// judge's order or report and recommendation (Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)).
event MagistrateObjectionServed() paper magistrate-objection
/// The notice of removal of a state court action is served (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 81.1(b)).
event RemovalNoticeServed()
/// The notice of removal of a state court action is filed (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 81.1(b)).
event RemovalNoticeFiled()
/// An attorney admitted to practice in the court is convicted of a felony
/// or other serious crime (Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(2)).
event AttorneyConvicted()
/// The court issues an order of discipline and conjoined order to show
/// cause on reciprocal discipline (Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(3)(A)).
event ReciprocalDisciplineOrderIssued()
/// The reviewing judge issues an order to show cause in an original
/// disciplinary proceeding (Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)(B)).
event DisciplineShowCauseIssued()
/// The reviewing judge's proposed determination is served on the attorney
/// (Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)(E)).
event ProposedDeterminationServed()
/// The withdrawing attorney files proof of service of the withdrawal order
/// on the client (Loc. Civ. R. 83.6(c)(2)).
event WithdrawalServiceProofFiled()

/// Loc. Civ. R. 4.1: within 30 days of the filing of the complaint, the
/// plaintiff files a status report on whether service of the summons and
/// complaint has been effectuated or waived by each defendant, unless it
/// has filed proof of service under FRCP 4(l) within those 30 days.
deadline service-status-report-period: 30.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 4.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 5.1(e): anyone who disputes the authenticity of a signature
/// on an electronically filed document files an objection within ten days
/// of receipt of the document or notice of its filing, whichever first
/// occurs.
deadline signature-objection-period: 10.days after ElectronicFilingReceived() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 5.1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(c)(1): the responding party serves and files its
/// response brief, with its supporting materials, within 21 days after
/// service of the moving party's memorandum. A failure to respond may be
/// deemed consent to the motion, except on summary judgment (Loc. Civ. R.
/// 7.1(f)).
deadline response-brief-period: 21.days after MotionMemorandumServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(3): the moving party may submit a reply brief within
/// 14 days after service of the responding party's memorandum.
deadline reply-brief-period: 14.days after ResponseMemorandumServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 7.1(b)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 15.1(b): unless the court orders otherwise, the moving
/// party files and serves a complete clean copy of the amended or
/// supplemental pleading within ten days of the order granting the motion.
deadline amended-pleading-period: 10.days after AmendmentGranted() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 15.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 16.1(a): at least 21 days before the time and date set for
/// the scheduling conference, counsel confer and discuss the items on the
/// litigation plan and discovery plan forms.
deadline litigation-plan-conference-period: 21.days before SchedulingConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 16.4(c)(1)(A): unless otherwise ordered, no later than 5
/// days before the Rule 16 scheduling conference, the parties meet and
/// confer about ADR.
deadline adr-conference-period: 5.days before SchedulingConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.4(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(a): unless otherwise ordered, not less than 30
/// calendar days before trial is scheduled to commence, each party provides
/// to the others and files its witnesses, deposition designations and
/// exhibits.
deadline trial-submissions-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c): within 7 days a party may file a response
/// memorandum to the opposing parties' trial memoranda. The rule names no
/// trigger; the period is read to run from service of the trial memorandum
/// it answers.
deadline trial-response-period: 7.days after TrialMemorandumServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 16.3(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 47.1(a): not less than 7 days before trial, attorneys may
/// submit written requests for voir dire questions.
deadline voir-dire-request-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 47.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 51.1(a): in a jury trial, written proposed jury
/// instructions and any request for special interrogatories and special
/// verdict forms are filed at least 14 days before trial; the court may
/// receive additional requests during trial.
deadline jury-instruction-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 51.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 51.1(b): the adverse party specifies its objections to the
/// requested instructions at least one day before trial.
deadline jury-instruction-objection-period: 1.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 51.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.3: when a civil action has been settled or otherwise
/// disposed of, counsel inform the clerk by 3 p.m. of the business day
/// immediately before trial, or costs, including one day's juror fees, may
/// be assessed.
deadline jury-settlement-notice-period: 1.court_days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(a)(1): within 14 days after entry of a judgment under
/// which costs may be claimed, the prevailing party serves and files a cost
/// bill in the local form, after the parties have met and conferred.
deadline cost-bill-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(a)(2): within 14 days after service of a cost bill,
/// any other party may serve and file specific objections.
deadline cost-objection-period: 14.days after CostBillServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(c)(1): review of the clerk's taxation is sought by a
/// motion to retax served and filed not later than 7 days after the clerk
/// taxes costs, under FRCP 54(d).
deadline retax-motion-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(c): within 21 days after receipt of a motion for
/// allowance of attorney fees, any other party may serve and file a
/// response brief stating specific grounds of objection.
deadline fee-response-period: 21.days after FeeMotionReceived() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(d): within 14 days after receipt of a response brief,
/// the moving party may submit a reply brief.
deadline fee-reply-period: 14.days after FeeResponseReceived() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(a): a motion for attorney fees under 42 U.S.C. §§
/// 406(b) or 1383(d)(2) is filed within 30 days of counsel's receipt of the
/// last Notice of Award needed to calculate the retroactive benefits.
deadline social-security-fee-motion-period: 30.days after LastNoticeOfAwardReceived() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c): the claimant or the defendant may file a response
/// brief within 21 days after receipt of the motion.
deadline social-security-fee-response-period: 21.days after SocialSecurityFeeMotionReceived() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c): claimant's counsel may submit a reply brief within
/// 14 days of any response brief.
deadline social-security-fee-reply-period: 14.days after SocialSecurityFeeResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 54.4(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1): under FRCP 72(a), a party may serve and file
/// objections to a magistrate judge's nondispositive order within 14 days
/// after being served with it, unless the magistrate judge or district
/// judge sets a different period.
deadline magistrate-order-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(2): under FRCP 72(b), a party serves and files
/// specific written objections to a magistrate judge's report and
/// recommendation within 14 days after being served with it, unless the
/// magistrate judge or district judge sets a different period.
deadline magistrate-report-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateReportServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(2)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1), (2): a party may serve and file a response to
/// another party's objections within 14 days after being served with them.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 72.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 81.1(b): in a removed action, if no response to a motion
/// pending in the state court was filed there, the response is due 21 days
/// after service of the notice of removal; the filing date of the notice is
/// the filing date of every pending motion, unless otherwise ordered.
deadline removed-motion-response-period: 21.days after RemovalNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 81.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 81.1(b): if a response was filed in the state court but no
/// reply, the reply is due 14 days after the filing of the notice of
/// removal.
deadline removed-motion-reply-period: 14.days after RemovalNoticeFiled() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 81.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(2): an attorney admitted to practice in the court
/// who is convicted of a felony or other serious crime reports the
/// conviction to the court within 14 days of its entry.
deadline conviction-report-period: 14.days after AttorneyConvicted() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(2)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(3)(A): an attorney who contends that the discipline
/// imposed by a supervising court should not be imposed here files a
/// petition to set it aside, or to be reinstated, within 30 days of the
/// court's order.
deadline reciprocal-discipline-petition-period: 30.days after ReciprocalDisciplineOrderIssued() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)(B): an attorney against whom an order to show
/// cause issues in an original disciplinary proceeding has 30 days from
/// the date of the order to file a response; omitting a request for a
/// hearing waives it.
deadline discipline-response-period: 30.days after DisciplineShowCauseIssued() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)(E): the attorney has 10 days from service of the
/// proposed determination to file a reply; absent a reply, the proposed
/// determination is entered as the final order.
deadline proposed-determination-reply-period: 10.days after ProposedDeterminationServed() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 83.5(b)(4)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Loc. Civ. R. 83.6(c)(2): the client has 21 days after the withdrawing
/// attorney files proof of service of the withdrawal order to advise the
/// court in writing how it will be represented; failing to appear within
/// that period is grounds for default or dismissal with prejudice.
deadline withdrawal-representation-period: 21.days after WithdrawalServiceProofFiled() counted_by frcp6-idaho cite "Dist. Idaho Loc. Civ. R. 83.6(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}
